// ================================================================
// ETPL_main.pdt — Self-Hosting Module Orchestrator
// ================================================================
// Version:    1.4.9 [Full-Trace Edition]
// Author:     Michael James Muller (Exception Theory)
// Purpose:    Assembles all 40 modules into a single unified
//             ETPL source via // @ETPL:import preprocessing.
//             When compiled, this file produces the self-hosted
//             ETPL binary with zero Python/C runtime dependencies.
//
// @ETPL:version 1.4.9
// @ETPL:entry-point main
// @ETPL:self-hosted true
// @ETPL:self-contained true
// @ETPL:full-trace true
// @ETPL:modular true
// @ETPL:module-id ETPL_main
//
// ET Master Equation:  P ∘ D ∘ T = E
// Tautological form:   3 = 3 = 3 = S
//
// ET Derivation -- full modular assembly:
//   P (40 individual .pdt module files -- infinite descriptor potential)
//   o
//   D (this file -- finite ordered @ETPL:import constraint manifold)
//   o
//   T (preprocessing traversal -- bounded by MANIFOLD_SYMMETRY^2 = 144)
//   =
//   E (unified ETPL source -- the self-hosted binary exception)
//
// ET Traverser Finiteness (Eq 219): the visited set in
// ETPLParser__preprocess_imports prevents any module from being
// included more than once, enforcing pragma-once semantics across
// all 40 imports regardless of nesting depth.
//
// Module count:    40 source files
// Source lines:    44,520 (+4 inter-module blank lines = 44,524)
// Entry point:     main()  (defined in ETPL_source.pdt)
//
// Build commands:
//   # Bootstrap interpret (Python host, no compilation)
//   python ETPL.py interpret ETPL_main.pdt
//
//   # Bootstrap compile → native binary (requires llvmlite)
//   python ETPL.py compile ETPL_main.pdt ETPL_selfhosted.exe
//
//   # Stage 1 self-compilation (binary compiles itself)
//   ETPL_selfhosted.exe compile ETPL_main.pdt ETPL_gen2.exe
//
// ================================================================


// ================================================================
// STAGE 0: BOOTSTRAP HEADER
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:module-begin ETPL_header 1-of-40
//
// Metadata-only module. Carries the @ETPL:entry-point annotation
// and all top-level build descriptors for the full binary.
//
// ET Identity Principle (Eq 211): the header is a pure D-descriptor
// that bounds the identity of the assembled binary. It produces no
// E-output of its own -- it is the binding constraint under which
// all other modules execute.
//
// Dependencies: none
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:import ETPL_header.pdt
// @ETPL:module-end ETPL_header


// ================================================================
// STAGE 1: ET NATIVE SUBSTRATE -- MATH
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:module-begin ET_Math_Native 2-of-40
//
// Closes the math C-extension gap (import math → ET_Math_Native).
// Provides: et_sin, et_cos, et_tan, et_sqrt, et_exp, et_log,
//           et_floor, et_ceil, et_pow, et_fabs, et_gamma, et_erf,
//           ET_PI, ET_E, ET_TAU, ET_PHI, ET_INF, ET_NAN,
//           and all remaining math.* equivalents.
//
// ET Descriptor Gap Principle (Eq 211): every symbol previously
// provided by the math C-extension is now bound via ET-native
// Taylor/Leibniz/Machin series derivations from the three axioms:
//   MANIFOLD_SYMMETRY = 12
//   BASE_VARIANCE = 1/12
//   KOIDE_RATIO = 2/3
//
// Dependencies: none (axiom-derived -- no imports)
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:import ET_Math_Native.pdt
// @ETPL:module-end ET_Math_Native


// ================================================================
// STAGE 2: ET NATIVE SUBSTRATE -- PLATFORM / SYS / TIME / MARSHAL
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:module-begin ET_Platform_Native 3-of-40
//
// Closes the sys, posix, time, and marshal C-extension gaps.
// Provides: et_exit, et_getcwd, et_getpid, et_listdir,
//           et_mkdir, et_unlink, et_rename, et_stat,
//           et_time, et_monotonic, et_sleep, et_gmtime,
//           ET_Marshal (etb_dumps, etb_loads, etb_header),
//           and all sys/posix/time/marshal equivalents.
//
// ET P ∘ D ∘ T = E: platform resources are D-addressed via
// hardware_access ∘ <addr-string>, eliminating all C-extension
// calls from the compiled binary.
//
// Dependencies: ET_Math_Native.pdt (for numeric operations)
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:import ET_Platform_Native.pdt
// @ETPL:module-end ET_Platform_Native


// ================================================================
// STAGE 3: ET NATIVE SUBSTRATE -- RUNTIME (STRING / IO / CLI)
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:module-begin ET_Runtime_Native 4-of-40
//
// Provides: et_strlen, et_strcmp, et_strncmp, et_strcpy, et_strcat,
//           et_strip_newline, CMD_* dispatch constants, et_cli_dispatch.
//
// These string primitives are used by trace files and ETPL_source.pdt
// for command parsing, error formatting, and CLI dispatch.
//
// ET P ∘ D ∘ T = E (string operations):
//   P = raw character substrate
//   D = length/compare/copy constraint
//   T = character-by-character traversal (bounded by string length)
//   E = grounded string result
//
// Dependencies: ET_Math_Native.pdt, ET_Platform_Native.pdt
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:import ET_Runtime_Native.pdt
// @ETPL:module-end ET_Runtime_Native


// ================================================================
// STAGE 4: LLVM IR EMISSION METHODS
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:module-begin LLVM_IR_Emission_Methods 5-of-40
//
// Provides: ET-native LLVM IR emission helpers used by the
// compiler backend in ETPL_source.pdt (ETPLCompiler class).
// These are the ET-translated equivalents of the LLVM IR
// builder method calls -- binding the compiler's D-descriptor
// constraints to the LLVM IR substrate.
//
// ET P ∘ D ∘ T = E (IR emission):
//   P = LLVM IR module (infinite potential instruction space)
//   D = IR emission method (finite opcode constraint)
//   T = builder traversal over AST nodes
//   E = grounded IR text / llvmlite IR object
//
// Dependencies: ET_Math_Native.pdt, ET_Platform_Native.pdt
// ================================================================
// @ETPL:import LLVM_IR_Emission_Methods.pdt
// @ETPL:module-end LLVM_IR_Emission_Methods


// ================================================================
// STAGE 5: C-EXTENSION TRACES (LOWEST-LEVEL DEPENDENCY CLOSURE)
// ================================================================
// These trace modules provide the symbol and type maps for Python
// C-extension modules. They must be loaded before any stdlib trace
// that depends on them.
//
// ET Descriptor Gap Principle (Eq 211): each trace closes a specific
// C-extension D-gap -- the symbol is declared and typed in ETPL so
// that ETPL_source.pdt can reference it without an import call.
//
// ET P ∘ D ∘ T = E (C-extension closure):
//   P = C-extension ABI (opaque substrate)
//   D = trace module (finite symbol-table constraint)
//   T = one-time trace load (single traversal at startup)
//   E = symbols available in ETPL environment (grounded)
// ================================================================

